  "body": "Add `appendHTML()`, `prependHTML()`, `beforeHTML()`, `afterHTML()`, and `replaceWithHTML()`, alongside their `*Unsafe()` variants.\n\n`NonDocumentTypeChildNode` methods fail silently when the child has no parent, like their equivalent DOM methods, and fail with a `\"HierarchyRequestError\"` `DOMException` for an invalid parent (`Document`, hostless `DocumentFragment`, `template` element, or `html` element). `appendHTML()` and `prependHTML()` (and their `*Unsafe()` variants) also throw a `\"HierarchyRequestError\"` `DOMException` when called on an `html` element, as parsing a fragment with an `html` context element always produces both a `head` and a `body` element.\n\nNote that the new `NonDocumentTypeChildNode` methods are also exposed on `CharacterData`.\n\nRenamed \"set and filter HTML\" to \"filter and set HTML\" to be more consistent with the order of operations and with the newly added helper methods.\n\nCloses #10122\n\n- [x] At least two implementers are interested (and none opposed):\n   * Chrome\n   * Gecko (https://github.com/mozilla/standards-positions/issues/1370)\n- [x] [Tests](https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt) are written and can be reviewed and commented upon at:\n   * https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt/pull/60555\n- [x] [Implementation bugs](https://github.com/whatwg/meta/blob/main/MAINTAINERS.md#handling-pull-requests) are filed:\n   * Chromium: Implemented\n   * WebKit: https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=315741\n   * Gecko: https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=2043150\n- [x] Corresponding [HTML AAM](https://w3c.github.io/html-aam/) & [ARIA in HTML](https://w3c.github.io/html-aria/) issues & PRs: N/A\n- [x] [MDN issue](https://github.com/whatwg/meta/blob/main/MAINTAINERS.md#handling-pull-requests) is filed: Will be done as part of Blink shipping\n- [x] The top of this comment includes a [clear commit message]\n\n\n<!--\n    This comment and the below content is programmatically generated.\n    You may add a comma-separated list of anchors you'd like a\n    direct link to below (e.g. #idl-serializers, #idl-sequence):\n\n    Don't remove this comment or modify anything below this line.\n    If you don't want a preview generated for this pull request,\n    just replace the whole of this comment's content by \"no preview\"\n    and remove what's below.\n-->\n***\n<a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/12753/dynamic-markup-insertion.html\" title=\"Last updated on Oct 12, 2026, 9:41 AM UTC (49e5663)\">/dynamic-markup-insertion.html</a>  ( <a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/12753/877d614...49e5663/dynamic-markup-insertion.html\" title=\"Last updated on Oct 12, 2026, 9:41 AM UTC (49e5663)\">diff</a> )\n<a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/12753/index.html\" title=\"Last updated on Oct 12, 2026, 9:41 AM UTC (49e5663)\">/index.html</a>  ( <a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/12753/877d614...49e5663/index.html\" title=\"Last updated on Oct 12, 2026, 9:41 AM UTC (49e5663)\">diff</a> )\n<a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/12753/infrastructure.html\" title=\"Last updated on Oct 12, 2026, 9:41 AM UTC (49e5663)\">/infrastructure.html</a>  ( <a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/12753/877d614...49e5663/infrastructure.html\" title=\"Last updated on Oct 12, 2026, 9:41 AM UTC (49e5663)\">diff</a> )\n<a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/12753/parsing.html\" title=\"Last updated on Oct 12, 2026, 9:41 AM UTC (49e5663)\">/parsing.html</a>  ( <a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/12753/877d614...49e5663/parsing.html\" title=\"Last updated on Oct 12, 2026, 9:41 AM UTC (49e5663)\">diff</a> )",
